{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfqWoLdfx29vGjbA5E2rP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've held the sitting. The verdict is recorded and both acts it called for are committed. Before committing, I checked that the verdict file parses as a valid three-kind sitting using the kit's own parser.\n\n**Verdict** (`807076e4`, trailer `WI: WI-849`), written to `docs/reviews/wi-849-approval-act-in-lane/002-ADJUDICATE-e648cd9.md`:\n\n| Section | Result | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| `## amendment` | `VERDICT: MEANING rows=7` | Every row changed what it requires. The common thread: the merge slot now admits an in-lane approval act when an accepted verdict judging its own rows backs it, instead of requiring an adjudication-kind lane. Some rows also add new refusals: malformed scope cells, unreadable claims, and approvals recorded only in the act ledger. I'd approve every new text; each one matches the code (`acceptance_record.py:843-1060`, `kitlib/registry.py:400`, `kitlib/sitting.py`). |\n| `## first-approval` | `OUTCOME: APPROVE rows=1` | TC-331's 15 named tests all exist. They and their companion `test_handback.py` test passed in this session (76 passed). |\n| `## done-when` | `DONE-WHEN: BLESSED changes=4` | The scope moved: the check that refuses a verdict from the session that authored the rows was dropped, along with its test. I blessed the move because the owner already split it out as WI-857 (queued), whose Done-when covers exactly that check. Drafting another successor would duplicate it. |\n\n**Acts:**\n- **`bf9293a3`:** re-attested LLR-158, LLR-167, LLR-181, LLR-278, LLR-310, TC-218 and TC-278 with `--reattests` and no `--verdict`, since the LLR/TC rung is released. The snapshot went through without refusing, and no Status cell was touched.\n- **`8ae2ba0b`:** flipped TC-331 from Drafted to Approved, with `snapshot --approves \"docs/test/test-cases.toml=WI-849\"` in the same commit.\n\nThe related suites (`test_snapshot_readers`, `test_adjudicate_brief`, `test_bootstrap`, `test_done_when_blessing`) also passed: 257 tests. I didn't run the full smoke bar, because this sitting changed no code.\n\nNotes for whoever picks this up:\n- **Binding file left alone.** `002-ADJUDICATE-e648cd9.md.requested` is still uncommitted and still says `outcome = pending`. Recording the outcome is the coordinator's job, so I didn't touch it.\n- **Stale interface reference.** `docs/interface-reference.md`'s IF-091 entry still describes `lane_approval_refusal` as refusing every work branch that takes an approval act, and gives `merge_approval_refusal` an old `adjudication` parameter. The IF-091 row in `interfaces.toml` was already updated. This is a separate finding, not one of the rows I judged.\n- **Misplaced obligation.** TC-331 lists LLR-161 among the rows it verifies, but the rule it tests (an unreadable claim is never closed early) is written in LLR-158, not LLR-161. It's a placement smell, not a reason to return the row."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":717,"cache_read_input_tokens":168709,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":717},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0476b322-cdeb-4686-bdbd-8bdcf58c085b","uuid":"ecb0796f-e39f-4497-aa44-1503c7f4072d","timestamp":"2026-10-08T21:54:53.007Z","request_id":"req_011CfqWoLL4PH7hcpn9Q7v2z"}
